{"term":"tank","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:17a2f4f44b71f9137c","definition":"A closed container for liquids or gases.","example":"The propane is stored in these tanks.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":["glass cannon"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tank#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:e3d07edd820832ddf9","definition":"An open container or pool for storing water or other liquids.","example":"The contractors installed a new tank with gorgeous fish and corals.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":["glass cannon"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tank#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:3d100dca8aaf8a7460","definition":"A pond, pool, or small lake (either natural or artificial).","example":"The tanks are full and the grass is high.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":["glass cannon"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tank#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:eeadd7ba9f17e0dc64","definition":"The fuel reservoir of a vehicle.","example":"We have brought the van to a garage after we found a leak in the tank.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":["glass cannon"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tank#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:7084752a5112496643","definition":"The amount held by a container; a tankful.","example":"I burned three tanks of gas on the drive to New York.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":["glass cannon"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tank#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:a54912062b9dff270e","definition":"An armoured fighting vehicle, armed with a gun designed for direct fire, and moving on caterpillar tracks.","example":"The journalist mistook the self-propelled artillery vehicle for a tank.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["battle tank","combat tank","armour","tango"],"antonyms":["glass cannon"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tank#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:81cd81e00ff7726c3b","definition":"A reservoir or dam (as it is known in the rest of Australia).","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":["glass cannon"],"collocations":[],"usage":"India","register":"India","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tank#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:24223581c8e2876e85","definition":"A structure of tightly overlapping leaves used by some bromeliads to retain water.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":["glass cannon"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tank#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:6c71779db05fdd8654","definition":"A very muscular and physically imposing person; somebody who is built like a tank.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":["glass cannon"],"collocations":[],"usage":"colloquial","register":"colloquial","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tank#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:637c6ea98fe638f11d","definition":"A bouncer or doorman.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":["glass cannon"],"collocations":[],"usage":"UK, broadly, dated, slang","register":"UK, broadly, dated, slang","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tank#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:8fb78acc0a4100cff4","definition":"A unit or character designed primarily around damage absorption and holding the attention of the enemy (as opposed to dealing damage, healing, or other tasks).","example":"The paladin can make for a decent tank, but I recommend that you get a class with better taunting skills.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":["glass cannon"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tank#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:ce7520b1c77bcbfa10","definition":"A prison cell, or prison generally.","example":"drunk tank","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":["glass cannon"],"collocations":[],"usage":"US, slang","register":"US, slang","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tank#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:15c4b21a776e2080ad","definition":"A metaphorical place where a player goes to contemplate a decision; see in the tank.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":["glass cannon"],"collocations":[],"usage":"slang","register":"slang","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tank#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:768f0203fcbe9cb94a","definition":"Ellipsis of tank engine or tank locomotive.","example":"Before their conversion to 4-6-0 tender locomotives, the L.B. & S.C.R. Baltic tank engines Nos. 330 to 334 measured 50 ft. 5 in. over buffers; the nearest present approach to this figure is the 49 ft. 10½ in. of the remaining ex-Lancashire & Yorkshire Hughes type 4-cylinder 4-6-4 tanks of the L.M.S.R. The Furness and G. & S.W.R. 4-6-4 tanks of the same company, all now scrapped, were, respectively, 49 ft. 1½ in. and 47 ft. 8 in. long.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":["glass cannon"],"collocations":[],"usage":"abbreviation, alt-of, ellipsis","register":"abbreviation, alt-of, ellipsis","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tank#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:9cf415af709dd453eb","definition":"Ellipsis of tank top.","example":"T-BACK COTTON TANK","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":["glass cannon"],"collocations":[],"usage":"abbreviation, alt-of, ellipsis","register":"abbreviation, alt-of, ellipsis","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tank#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:d1bf5217ecf7afbbcc","definition":"To fail or fall (often used in describing the economy or the stock market); to degenerate or decline rapidly; to plummet.","example":"He told me about all the odd jobs he'd taken after I was born, when Michigan's economy was tanking. For one, he crisscrossed the Midwest buying old carpets from dentists' offices.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["tank up","face tank","buay tank"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tank#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:5b73df5c729d85f329","definition":"To attract the attacks of an enemy target in cooperative team-based combat, so that one's teammates can defeat the enemy in question more efficiently.","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["tank up","face tank","buay tank"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tank#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:5b6baf08a6d2c40213","definition":"To put (fuel, etc.) into a tank.","example":"Concrete below ground must be fully tanked to prevent water uptake.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["tank up","face tank","buay tank"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tank#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:43e03b72a03d6bf86e","definition":"To deliberately lose a sports match with the intent of gaining a perceived future competitive advantage.","example":"Beforehand, Swedish [national ice hockey team] coach Bengt-Ake Gustafsson had ruminated about tanking against Slovakia to avoid powerful Canada or the Czechs in the quarters [i.e., quarterfinals of the 2006 Winter Olympic tournament], telling Swedish television, \"One is cholera, the other the plague.\"","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["tank up","face tank","buay tank"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tank#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:94fae48e5aff3127c5","definition":"To resist damage; to be attacked without being hurt.","example":"Unless Bane can tank Helicarrier-busting explosions I'm not sure how he stands a chance.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"slang","register":"slang","wordFamily":["tank up","face tank","buay tank"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tank#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:ab61852b74fc242007","definition":"To contemplate a decision for a long time; to go in the tank.","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"slang","register":"slang","wordFamily":["tank up","face tank","buay tank"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tank#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:29c368e54febb70336","definition":"To stand; to tolerate.","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"Singapore, colloquial","register":"Singapore, colloquial","wordFamily":["tank up","face tank","buay tank"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tank#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:6d61b90857e3b97c79","definition":"To willingly take on an undesirable task or burden.","example":"","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"Singapore, colloquial","register":"Singapore, colloquial","wordFamily":["tank up","face tank","buay tank"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tank#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:c57ec017384fb6ef2d","definition":"A small Indian dry measure, averaging 240 grains in weight.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["tank 